            <ArticleTitle>[Use of the excimer laser in experimental laser angioplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>238-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>XeCl-excimer laser produce pulsed far uv-light (wave length lambda = 308 nm). Biophysical effects were studied on arteriosclerotic human cadaver aortic and coronary vessels. Ablative photodecomposition results in cleanliness of the incisions with minimal thermal side effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
